          <detaileddescription>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Describes the structural role of a node in a scene layout. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>A layout is represented as a tree of <ref refid="structfccvis_1_1scene_1_1meta_1_1LayoutNode" kindref="compound">LayoutNode</ref> objects. Each node has one of three structural roles:</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>Pack:</computeroutput> contains child nodes arranged according to an orientation.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>Tab:</computeroutput> contains child nodes presented as alternative tab views.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>Leaf:</computeroutput> represents a concrete scene slot.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="structfccvis_1_1scene_1_1meta_1_1LayoutNode" kindref="compound">LayoutNode</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
